we're here at hillary clinton's  headquarters now going to talk to sue of  her senior advisors about the campaign  and about this headquarters and the  culture thereof joining us now amanda  rendrea is the national political  director marlon marshall is the director  of states we're gonna have to figure out  what that means in the course of this  interview that seems like it seems like  an awesome title somebody worked for  napoleon  uh amanda start with you  not everybody who's watching knows  you've got a big title a political  director's huge thing just tell us a  little bit about your political  background how you ended up as hillary  clinton's political director for this  campaign um well i think it does start  where i grew up in a small town  but i ended up becoming the first latina  chief of staff in the united states  senate and really got a chance to see  her as a senator and really watch her  career and watch a woman rise within the  senate but also in the political sphere  and no doubt um i love the idea of  breaking ceilings  what what presidential campaigns have  you worked on first first this is it  this is the first one okay but marlon  newton uh with president obama before  coming over to the clinton campaign i  was i was i got a chance to work at the  white house for the president uh prior  to actually started one of the reasons i  started my mom teacher 36 years  and was very involved in the political  process in terms of letting us know as  kids how we got to make sure that we are  participating in that process to make  sure that we are always fighting for  education so  i started right after college got  involved in campaigns got a chance to  work for the secretary 08 during her  first run and then the president on the  general election and the re-elect and  then like you said i got a chance to  work in the white house all right so  what is director of states  well we have obviously i have a support  role we have four fantastic state  directors in iowa new hampshire nevada  and south carolina my job is to make  sure they get what they need to run very  distinct state programs that we're  building a  volunteer infrastructure in iowa that's  going to help us win iowa caucus that  we're building infrastructure new  hampshire is going to reach out to  voters and make sure we're successful in  the amsterdam primary they're great my  job is helping make sure they get what  they need so one of the reasons we're  excited to be here today is this  headquarters has not been up and running  very long it hadn't been open to the  press very much but we were allowed to  walk around talk to your some of your  colleagues all day um everybody seems to  be in a pretty good mood and seems even  though it's a young campaign and there  are a lot of people here just working  together first time  the spirit seems pretty good i'm just  wondering you all done politics before  how would you characterize kind of the  ethos of this particular campaign  i think you can feel it as you go around  it's interesting it's creative it's we  really are trying to push the envelope  of give us your ideas and let's try it  out  i think what you see is really a  creative energy um but also we're  working for a candidate who has worked  for a long time on fighting for issues  that a lot of folks here have cared  about and um you can feel that you can  feel that in the fight every day when  people are waking up saying how do i  help yeah what do we do differently how  do we make it work  and really across the different  organizations we all work together not  just in silos but across the various  organizations and that's fun and we're  very deliberate about culture probably  seeing as you walked around there's a  document that lists out some of the  culture and principles that this  campaign lives by and that comes from  her being very deliberate making sure we  have a good time that we're working for  the right reasons uh and that we all are  working together and so we're very  deliberate about that and you can feel  as you walk around there's a crazy  emphasis on health food here  i see lots of signs with fresh fruit and  vegetables who's had pizza  it's because we have pizza so much that  seeing some of the healthy stuff makes  you feel at least like you're learning  something even if you're not eating it  if you walk over by our section you'll  see grapes bananas if you walk in my  office you don't see that so why don't  we might have had cupcakes today  like 12 different ones right the  smallest i was going to say i ducked in  the gym by mary's office for the  jalapeno chips  that's right good though  there's a ton of people here i mean  you've never done a presidential you've  been involved in lots of possibilities  there's a ton of people here working on  their first campaign yeah i'm just  wondering from each of you marla stark  what's what's that what's the thing you  tell people about how to do this for the  people who've never done it before well  one i think even when you start the  interview process you just be realistic  about what you're going to get into and  make sure you're doing it for the right  reasons you're ready to work uh several  hours a day and so really kind of again  you gotta dig into why someone want to  work here what are the values they have  do those values match the values of the  campaign frankly the candidate  everyone here you feel that way  so just making sure again they're doing  it for right reasons they always remind  themselves their own personal story  because that's what's gonna only thing  that's gonna keep you going every day i  always i literally call my mom or text  her every other day be like this went  well they're like oh tough day mom but  and she's gonna want to kind of keep me  going um and so you gotta remind folks  why they're here every day you're not  gonna impress a lot of moms by saying  you text her every day every other day  every other year  yeah as a mom  right what just tells you she texts me  when one sort of political rule you tell  the younger people here um so two things  actually i say don't forget the wire  here  and remember on this roller coaster  it really is on the one hand we're doing  something really big for our country on  the other hand don't forget to enjoy the  moment every single day  because after the campaign is over i  think a lot of people goes by so fast in  a lot of ways  that there are these moments on a  campaign that  really do change people's life where  they remember them forever  and we try our best to do both of that  remember the gravity of what we're doing  really the seriousness of what we're  doing and at the same time  look around and breathe in and enjoy it  yeah campaigns are really about their  family you spend a lot of time each  other i met my wife for the campaign  2004 john kerry uh so be in the moment  and and know that's a very it's very  powerful  you know talking about family and  texting here mom and parents you know  i'm curious  but i'm curious to know a little bit  more about your father and his role in  terms of helping you  in the way that you think about some of  the issues from the campaign for some of  our watchers who might not know your  father did immigrate from mexico in the  1960s before you were born you were born  in california but um and i'm wondering  uh immigration has will be a big issue  in the campaign and already has become  such a hot-button issue uh and not just  immigration but mexico because of some  of donald trump's recent comments um  how has your father's background  affected how you think about this and is  that something that that he has talked  about what impact do you think  some of trump's remarks have had so far  um i would just say the impact on my  life in general when you come from  parents my dad was from sakatecas mexico  and my mom was from california but they  all they both work in the fields and  when you realize that somebody works so  hard for you to have the opportunities  in life  it truly is at your core and in  everything you do and being able to be  as blessed as i've been to be able to  have the opportunities i've had  it's never lost on me that there's some  kid  whether it's like my dad just wanting to  make a better life for somebody else or  growing up figuring out how do i make my  parents proud for all the hard work they  did and so when you hear something like  what trump says it really gets to at  least someone like me at the core of  what i believe this country is great for  and why i'm even working on this  campaign  and what i've said about it is it used  to be an honor i used to say it's an  honor to be a national political  director  because we're trying to build the  biggest tent that's ever been built and  being welcoming to everyone  but it's really become much more of a  responsibility to me  that i really do want everyone to feel  like  the like our campaign the democratic  party we're here we welcome you and we  give you honor and want you to succeed  in life what's your dad's analysis on uh  on donald trump  well my dad my dad well you know he  taught us all girls how to punch and so  you can imagine what he thought if i  came across a makeup be ready you know  be ready to fight um but you know  you know i think i think it's a little  bit hurtful i think he probably views it  from the eyes of my boys i have now boys  who are growing up right and what do  they think about being mexican and i  think he's a little softer in his older  age he tells me to still punch but he  tells them like it's okay it's going to  be okay we're going to build a better  world for you  um so it's been it's been interesting to  see sort of the reaction um and i think  even more so i think they understand  what i'm doing and why it's important  that we build the biggest tent we  possibly can in this election last  question for you your states  rise of bernie sanders senator sanders  doing pretty well yeah can he not willie  but can he beat hillary clinton in  either iowa new hampshire or both  first of all we always expected the  competitive primary i've heard that line  i'm representing  there's a true lie it's a true line  i think we have the staff out there that  are building a fantastic organization  they're going to continue to build that  organization and i think you'll see us  be successful in the iowa caucus and new  hampshire prime minister you don't want  to say where you can win  i think we're going to be successful and  win this uh primary campaign looking  forward to it all right  as you go around the country and spend  time in presidential campaign stats  you'll see regardless democrats  republicans people like this who  care about their candidate care about  their country working really hard thank  you both for joining us thank you  appreciate amanda andrea and marlon  marshall

